      "problem": "Find the value of the expression $\\sqrt{ (3^4+7^2-2) \\div 2}.$",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate the given expression, we use PEMDAS. In terms of the order of operations: \n\n- expressions underneath radicals are treated the same as parentheses\n\n- radicals themselves are treated as exponents\n\nTherefore, following the order of operations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{({3}^{4}+{7}^{2}-2)÷2} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{(81+49-2)÷2} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{(130-2)÷2} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{128÷2} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{64} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{8\\cdot 8} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{8}^{2}} & = \\\\ 8 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
